                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "042a9f66-2010-3622-a8f6-67e18c104e57",
                        "entry_id": "b85c0f5d-28ce-3082-8c60-e6b59ff6c773",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conveyance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb9081ff-260d-3104-896d-393c085cfa64",
                        "entry_id": "b85c0f5d-28ce-3082-8c60-e6b59ff6c773",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An accusation or charge brought against someone, especially by an informer; the act of accusing someone."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6878d150-d06e-4cf8-8992-b7d8b9bece72",
                                "sense_id": "bb9081ff-260d-3104-896d-393c085cfa64",
                                "text": "Some curious circumstances respecting delation, prison life, and autos da fe are here minutely recorded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb7748c0-e422-4a69-9336-f527876988b7",
                                "sense_id": "bb9081ff-260d-3104-896d-393c085cfa64",
                                "text": "Such public defiance might become Valentinian; but it could leave no room for the unworthy delation of the philosopher Maximus, which supposes some more private offence, (Zosimus, l. iv. p. 200, 201.)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f16ce433-a418-4b6a-910e-db7c17e0e0c1",
                                "sense_id": "bb9081ff-260d-3104-896d-393c085cfa64",
                                "text": "A wise woman who was popular with her neighbours might escape delation; whereas one who had fallen out with them might find herself accused not just of charming, but even of black witchcraft."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b33576a-b322-4b82-9f49-e81109b88e04",
                                "sense_id": "bb9081ff-260d-3104-896d-393c085cfa64",
                                "text": "2012, Bradford E. Hinze, Chapter 1: A Decade of Disciplining Theologians, Richard R. Gaillardetz (editor), When the Magisterium Intervenes, Liturgical Press (Michael Glazier), page 9,\nDelations frequently come from a local bishop, but there have been cases where vigilante groups (e.g., Catholics United for the Faith) and individuals have complained about a theologian's writings or lectures."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a947bae3-de48-428b-9a15-642cc4653bb0",
                        "source_entry_id": "b85c0f5d-28ce-3082-8c60-e6b59ff6c773",
                        "source_sense_description": "accusation — see also accusation",
                        "target_lang_word": "délation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "délation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                        "entry_id": "aad6cfb6-b6d1-3fde-a26a-9cebda245138",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dénonciation faite dans un mauvais dessein (obtenir un avantage quelconque, tel de l’argent)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e38d3bde-f523-4714-b2fd-424cda60b2b0",
                                                "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                                "text": "Cette anonyme délation, qui accusait le prince et ma femme, part encore d’une main ennemie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0b34367-5c5c-4214-9485-3a7aedf29abb",
                                                "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                                "text": "Le Marquis.– Il y a des circonstances où la délation, s’appuyant sur un dévouement sans bornes, devient de l’abnégation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78bfcc78-d861-4dd3-b0ae-45cbc8c09bed",
                                                "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                                "text": "Un excellent moyen d’avancement, c’est la délation. Cela vous met bien avec la police, qui tout aussitôt vous protège, mais en se servant de vous ; car une fois que l’on a commencé, il n’y a plus d’honneur ou d’amitié qui tienne : il faut marcher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a3986c8-5291-4fe5-b2f3-2531342b8112",
                                                "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                                "text": "Chaque fois que la délation est érigée en système, chaque fois elle sert à de tragiques règlements de comptes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ba28a0f-7c5e-4eb7-ab3e-72713499db22",
                                                "sense_id": "59b96025-3a72-3978-8946-b04497605e5f",
                                                "text": "La deuxième façon d’appeler à la délation est de la valoriser comme un devoir citoyen, civique. Ce n’est plus de la délation, c’est de la dénonciation dans le sens où c’est pour aider l’État, la population."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
